WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.142
Real data rarely arrives perfectly clean.

00:00:03.142 --> 00:00:07.617
The small sales example contains several realistic problems.

00:00:07.617 --> 00:00:10.992
Some text values contain extra spaces.

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:14.777
Some use uppercase while others use lowercase.

00:00:14.777 --> 00:00:17.847
Currency values include dollar signs.

00:00:17.847 --> 00:00:24.387
One date is invalid. Some fields are missing, and one order appears more than once.

00:00:24.387 --> 00:00:26.992
None of these problems is unusual.

00:00:26.992 --> 00:00:33.205
The important skill is learning to recognize them systematically rather than fixing values randomly.

00:00:33.717 --> 00:00:37.519
Before cleaning, think about what each row represents.

00:00:37.519 --> 00:00:44.099
If one row is supposed to represent one order, then a repeated order I D may be a duplicate.

00:00:44.099 --> 00:00:50.414
But if one order can contain several line items, the repeated I D may be valid.

00:00:50.414 --> 00:00:53.205
Data cleaning always depends on meaning.
